    "body": "So `blob://test/` is a relative URL??\n\nTo be clear: the url field for a HTMLHyperlinkElementUtils contains a URL record. My assertion is that if the URL record's scheme is \"blob\", it's non-relative flag is always set, so you can remove the \"and its non-relative flag is set\". I'd be curious how you'd set up an `<a>` or `<area>` element so that its url record has a scheme blob but non-relative flag unset.\n",
    "created_at": "2016-02-10T16:52:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-02-10T19:23:54Z",
